 S~S Primary purpose of the file master-format-example

------------------------------------------

  SimpleSal documents produced for metadata purposes use this organization and with a very
  limited notation: Ascii character set; outline markers '=', '-' and '*'; "S~S" header tags.

  The reason that TSC LLC sets a low bar for expectations with respect to source control metadata
  is that the time and energy needed to create nicely-formatted content is beyond the basic task.

  The example demonstrates that the tools used to view and manipulate both the repo and the
  human metadata are the narrow funnel through which managed object versions are understood.

  Conformity enforced by the system is simplified down to a level any human or computer can meet.
  For example, a photographic image of a version number might not be parsable by some consumers.

